    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="0665" n="1499" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/505</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-03T12:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 3.29 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3000. Your 1343, June 1, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d554-f1"/> received today.
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs writes me <hi rendition="#italic">Hector</hi> and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Zijldijk</hi> have now received the German safe
                    conducts and are sailing today simultaneously with the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Java</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Stella</hi> from America.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
